## 🔍 4. Phase 2: Pre-Flight AWS Checks

Before building the cluster, always verify 3 things: your IAM credentials, your target region, and which EC2 instance types your AWS Free Tier account allows.

### Step 1: Verify Your AWS IAM User & Region
```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
aws configure get region
```
*Expected Output:*
```json
{
    "UserId": "AIDAZXJQWHNH4CCH7CD2Q",
    "Account": "668506405711",
    "Arn": "arn:aws:iam::668506405711:user/Practice_arafat"
}
ap-south-1
```

### Step 2: Check Allowed Free Tier Instance Types in Your Region
New AWS Free Tier accounts will **block** `t3.medium`! Run this command to see which instance types your account allows for free:
```bash
aws ec2 describe-instance-types \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --filters "Name=free-tier-eligible,Values=true" \
  --query "InstanceTypes[].[InstanceType,VCpuInfo.DefaultVCpus,MemoryInfo.SizeInMiB]" \
  --output table
```
*Expected Output:*
```text
+-----------------+----+--------+
|     DescribeInstanceTypes     |
+-----------------+----+--------+
|  t8i.micro      |  2 |  1024  |
|  t4g.small      |  2 |  2048  |
|  t3.micro       |  2 |  1024  |
|  c7i-flex.large |  2 |  4096  |  <-- BEST CHOICE (2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM)
|  t4g.micro      |  2 |  1024  |
|  m7i-flex.large |  2 |  8192  |
|  t3.small       |  2 |  2048  |
|  t8i.small      |  2 |  2048  |
+-----------------+----+--------+
```
> **Why we choose `c7i-flex.large`:** Micro instances (`t3.micro`) only have 1 GB RAM and can only run 4 pods total. `c7i-flex.large` is Free Tier-eligible, has 4 GB RAM, and supports up to 29 pods per node!

### Step 3: Check for Any Leftover Broken CloudFormation Stacks
```bash
aws cloudformation list-stacks \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --stack-status-filter CREATE_FAILED ROLLBACK_COMPLETE DELETE_FAILED \
  --query "StackSummaries[?starts_with(StackName, 'eksctl-')].[StackName,StackStatus]" \
  --output table
```
*(If the output is empty, your AWS account is clean and ready!)*

