### Problem 4: `ValidationError: cannot be deleted while TerminationProtection is enabled`

**❌ Error Message Seen:**
When we tried to delete the dead `ROLLBACK_COMPLETE` nodegroup stack so we could recreate it:
```text
root@ip-172-31-12-85:/home/ubuntu# aws cloudformation delete-stack \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --stack-name eksctl-my-eks-cluster-nodegroup-standard-workers

aws: [ERROR]: An error occurred (ValidationError) when calling the DeleteStack operation: Stack [eksctl-my-eks-cluster-nodegroup-standard-workers] cannot be deleted while TerminationProtection is enabled
```

**🔍 Why It Happened:**
By default, `eksctl` turns on **CloudFormation Termination Protection** on every stack it creates so nobody accidentally deletes it from the AWS Console.

**✅ How We Solved It:**
First, disable Termination Protection using `update-termination-protection`, and then delete the stack:
```bash
# 1. Disable Termination Protection on the failed stack
aws cloudformation update-termination-protection \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --no-enable-termination-protection \
  --stack-name eksctl-my-eks-cluster-nodegroup-standard-workers

# 2. Delete the failed stack
aws cloudformation delete-stack \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --stack-name eksctl-my-eks-cluster-nodegroup-standard-workers
```

